---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="How WageLark works"
	description="Where WageLark gets its facts, how pages are dated and corrected, and how it earns money."
>
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-[720px]">
		<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--navy)] md:text-4xl">How WageLark works</h1>

		<div class="prose-content mt-7 max-w-[640px] text-[0.9375rem] leading-[1.85] text-[var(--ink)]/70">
			<p>
				WageLark covers what a job pays, what it takes to get in and what the work involves, using
				government wage and employment data.
			</p>

			<h2>Sources</h2>
			<p>
				Each page lists the sources behind it, with links. Most come from the U.S. Bureau of Labor
				Statistics, O*NET, CareerOneStop, the Census Bureau and the Department of Labor. Every wage
				figure is labeled with its source and data year.
			</p>

			<h2>Dates and corrections</h2>
			<p>
				Every page shows when it was last updated. If something is wrong, write to
				<a href="mailto:contact@wagelark.com">contact@wagelark.com</a> with the page address and what
				looks off. Confirmed errors get fixed.
			</p>

			<h2>Ads and money</h2>
			<p>
				Pages carry display ads. No page is sponsored, and advertisers do not see or approve pages
				before they run. The <a href="/privacy/">Privacy page</a> lists the advertising and analytics
				services the site uses.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.prose-content :global(h2) {
		margin-top: 1.75rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--navy);
	}
	.prose-content :global(h2:first-child) {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	.prose-content :global(p) {
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	.prose-content :global(a) {
		color: var(--teal-dark);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}
</style>
